  "query_preview": "/SUNDAY THROUGH FRIDAY/...\nIssued at 326 PM CDT Fri Aug 14 2026\n\nSouthwesterly flow aloft will transition to westerly on Sunday \nas high pressure retrogrades west across Texas. Another round of\nthunderstorms is possible across the western half of the \nforecast area Sunday as the models initiate convection off to \nthe west of the forecast area. Steering winds will carry this \nactivity east southeast across southwestern Nebraska into \nnorthwestern Kansas. Limited CAPE across the eastern 2/3rds of \nthe forecast area along with weak mid level lapse rates, should \nkeep the severe threat across far western portions of the \nforecast area. West northwest flow aloft will persist through \nTuesday with daily chances for showers and thunderstorms across \nthe area. By Wednesday, the mid range solns. begin to amplify \nridging across the western CONUS. This will place the central \nand northern plains in more northwesterly flow aloft. This will \nlimit precipitation chances toward the end of next week. As for \ntemperatures, cooler air will back into the eastern forecast \narea next week with highs in the 70s Wednesday, Thursday and \nFriday. Highs will be in the lower to middle 80s in the west and\nsouthwestern forecast area.",
